\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Wrap bonds and correlations}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{The periodic picture in \ref{fdip-00HV} keeps the quadratic
diagonal and adds ferromagnetic couplings across opposite edges.
The periodic quartic measure studied by
\citek{bauerschmidt2024logsobolev} also has a different quadratic
counterterm. Which direction do these two changes move its
two-point correlations, and can the resulting upper bound remain
uniform while the mesh and square change?}
